# museo voice

## voice (anything a user sees)
No em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in UI, notifications, widgets, or AI-written output. Dashes read as machine-generated; muse never should.

Use instead:
- middle dot for separators: `9:41a · the thought`
- colon or comma for leads: `done: timer set for 20m`
- short sentences. two is enough.

Register: all lowercase, brief, warm, a perceptive friend. No exclamation marks, no marketing voice, no therapy-speak, no "don't forget".

Any LLM prompt in the app whose output a user reads must include "no dashes" (or stricter voice) in its instructions.

Code comments are exempt.

## museo build adds
- Page titles end with a period: "build with museo.", "your ring.", "firmware.".
- Dialogs ask a question and answer with verbs: "remove your ring?" with "remove" and "keep it"; "delete every muse?" with "delete everything".
- Ring words: **hold** (streaming; a muse made that way is streamed, never "live"), **double click** (memory), **click** (play or pause), **three clicks** (skip). Never "tap" or "press" for the ring.
- Accessibility labels, notifications, errors and model output (titles, notes) follow the same rules. Proper names the person said keep their case.
- System and library error text goes through `String.museQuiet` before it's shown. Model instructions start from `MuseAI.voice`; model output goes through `.museCalm`, which keeps the names they said.
- Purpose strings are lowercase and say exactly what the permission is for: "museo links to your ring over bluetooth to bring in what you say."

## naming

| Thing | Write | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| A recording turned into words | "a muse", "muses" | An empty one is "blank muse". |
| The app's wordmark | "museo." | `AppConfig.appName` plus a period, in Lora. |
| The ring | "your ring" in sentences, "museo" as its name | `AppConfig.ringName`. |
| The two ways in | "streaming" (hold), "memory" (double click) | `Muse.origin` `.stream` and `.offline`. |
| Notes | "notes" (bullets), "the thought" (a long one's write-up) | `MuseNotes.Kind` `.brief`, `.longThought`. |
| Platform words | "iphone", "bluetooth", "siri", "apple intelligence" | Lowercase in UI. |
| Places in the app | "build › speech", "ring sheet › firmware" | A `›` between steps. |
| Times | "9:41a", "2m ago", "yesterday", "wednesday october 8" | `museClock`, `museRelative`, `museDayTitle`. Never format dates by hand. |
| Durations | "0:12", "1:02:19" | `museDuration`. |
| Something in progress | "joining…", "writing it up…" | A real ellipsis character. |
| Ring states | "linked · 80%", "looking for your ring · click it to wake it", "bringing in 3" | Take them from `RingStatus` (MuseoKit). |
| A link that leaves the app | "open settings ↗" | End it with `↗`. |

## leave alone
The ring kit (`MuseoKit`, from GitHub `its4ff/museo-kit`) is not copy work. Its status lines come from `RingStatus`; don't edit the kit to change them.
